1
00:00:00,035 --> 00:00:03,605
Former Congressman Ramon dela Peña
remains at large.

2
00:00:03,605 --> 00:00:08,443
<i>Pieces of evidence show
that he is behind the murder</i>

3
00:00:08,443 --> 00:00:10,712
<i>of his personnel, Lando Nakpil.</i>

4
00:00:10,712 --> 00:00:13,481
<i>And to you, Ramon dela Peña,
your days are numbered.</i>

5
00:00:13,481 --> 00:00:15,283
- We've found it.
- Have you found Liam?

6
00:00:15,283 --> 00:00:16,304
The safe house.

7
00:00:16,304 --> 00:00:18,854
If something happens to your son,
he deserves it.

8
00:00:18,854 --> 00:00:20,240
I don't care!

9
00:00:20,240 --> 00:00:22,796
Your son should get what he deserves.

10
00:00:22,796 --> 00:00:24,326
Hans, do it now!

11
00:00:25,192 --> 00:00:26,428
Dad, go on! Help them escape.

12
00:00:26,428 --> 00:00:28,439
Call the police.

13
00:00:28,439 --> 00:00:29,951
Dad!

14
00:00:30,932 --> 00:00:33,333
- Mom, look out for Joyce!
- Joyce!

15
00:00:33,333 --> 00:00:36,052
- Joyce!
- Go ahead! Try it, Ramon.

16
00:00:59,393 --> 00:01:01,467
Are you following me?

17
00:01:07,537 --> 00:01:08,877
Joyce?

18
00:01:10,039 --> 00:01:12,259
What are you doing here?

19
00:01:13,342 --> 00:01:15,361
I'm on vacation.

20
00:01:17,446 --> 00:01:19,744
What about you? What are you doing here?

21
00:01:21,617 --> 00:01:24,182
I'm on vacation too.

22
00:01:28,191 --> 00:01:32,031
I forget that it is also
your dream to be in Paris.

23
00:01:34,909 --> 00:01:38,086
Whatever your reason is for coming here,

24
00:01:40,054 --> 00:01:42,056
I know it's not because of me.

25
00:01:48,644 --> 00:01:50,681
Do you want to take a walk?

26
00:02:07,463 --> 00:02:13,903
I took leave from the university
where I teach Creative Writing.

27
00:02:13,903 --> 00:02:17,339
I'm taking my chance
to finish writing a book here.

28
00:02:20,315 --> 00:02:21,716
A book?

29
00:02:22,914 --> 00:02:24,274
Yeah...

30
00:02:25,681 --> 00:02:28,484
Passion project. A novel.

31
00:02:34,657 --> 00:02:37,810
I'm glad you've fulfilled your dreams.

32
00:02:38,989 --> 00:02:41,163
Same with you, Joyce.

33
00:02:41,163 --> 00:02:45,458
Your advocacy projects make me feel proud.

34
00:02:50,973 --> 00:02:55,552
By the way, Joyce, I sent the...

35
00:02:56,545 --> 00:02:59,115
The annulment papers to your house.

36
00:02:59,115 --> 00:03:02,028
I didn't know you are here in Paris.

37
00:03:04,335 --> 00:03:08,927
My mom told me about the papers.

38
00:03:15,231 --> 00:03:18,734
I will sign when I get home.

39
00:03:20,201 --> 00:03:21,608
Is it okay?

40
00:03:25,041 --> 00:03:27,310
Is it okay to what?

41
00:03:27,310 --> 00:03:29,436
Is it okay...

42
00:03:31,314 --> 00:03:34,077
that I filed our annulment papers?

43
00:03:39,488 --> 00:03:41,590
Yes.

44
00:03:42,558 --> 00:03:45,695
We've been separated for three years.

45
00:03:45,695 --> 00:03:49,097
It's just a formality.
There's no problem with it.

46
00:03:49,999 --> 00:03:52,937
- But since we're already here...
- But...

47
00:03:56,005 --> 00:03:57,573
Okay, go ahead.

48
00:03:57,573 --> 00:03:59,608
You go first.

49
00:03:59,608 --> 00:04:01,276
- You go first.
- Go ahead.

50
00:04:04,180 --> 00:04:05,581
Sorry.

51
00:04:10,219 --> 00:04:11,663
Hello, love?

52
00:04:16,398 --> 00:04:17,694
Yes...

53
00:04:19,033 --> 00:04:20,534
Yes.

54
00:04:33,542 --> 00:04:35,277
Okay. I'll just fix...

55
00:04:35,277 --> 00:04:38,329
I'll sign the papers when I get back
to the Philippines.

56
00:04:43,719 --> 00:04:46,789
No... I'm busy.

57
00:04:46,789 --> 00:04:49,558
Can I call you later?

58
00:05:19,094 --> 00:05:20,563
My son...

59
00:05:21,857 --> 00:05:26,828
You didn't warn me
that I'd see your dad here.

60
00:05:27,930 --> 00:05:31,533
How can we move on, my son?

61
00:05:38,307 --> 00:05:40,546
But, son, you know...

62
00:05:44,613 --> 00:05:47,282
I'm happy for him.

63
00:05:50,352 --> 00:05:54,390
I'm happy to see that
he has fulfilled all his dreams.

64
00:05:54,390 --> 00:05:58,610
Maybe I was the one dragging him down.

65
00:06:02,998 --> 00:06:05,973
But why am I being like this?

66
00:06:10,172 --> 00:06:14,309
I have also fulfilled all my dreams, right?

67
00:06:16,920 --> 00:06:19,514
Now, we're here.

68
00:06:20,416 --> 00:06:23,451
I'm here in Paris, my son.

69
00:06:27,037 --> 00:06:30,759
Now, I'm here in...

70
00:06:30,759 --> 00:06:33,928
I'm here in the city of love.

71
00:06:45,374 --> 00:06:48,912
While your dad is calling someone...

72
00:06:50,045 --> 00:06:52,783
He's calling someone "love".

73
00:06:55,963 --> 00:06:58,087
But, son...

74
00:06:58,087 --> 00:07:00,189
Your mom isn't affected by it.

75
00:07:00,189 --> 00:07:02,023
I'm really not.

76
00:07:04,033 --> 00:07:08,464
Your dad is free to do anything.

77
00:07:08,464 --> 00:07:12,300
Anything that can make him happy.

78
00:07:15,471 --> 00:07:18,608
I have no right to stop him.

79
00:07:21,477 --> 00:07:23,171
I no longer have the right.

80
00:07:30,085 --> 00:07:32,686
I hope you understand.

81
00:07:35,330 --> 00:07:37,765
I miss you.

82
00:07:41,130 --> 00:07:43,716
I love you, son.

83
00:08:02,351 --> 00:08:04,453
Bonjour! Je m'appelle Mark.

84
00:08:04,453 --> 00:08:07,923
So, I will be your tour guide today.

85
00:08:07,923 --> 00:08:11,927
Put your name tags and armbands on,
so we won't lose each other.

86
00:08:11,927 --> 00:08:15,197
We're here in
one of the busiest places in Paris.

87
00:08:15,197 --> 00:08:17,866
So, Mr. Gerald and I
are both wearing white bands.

88
00:08:17,866 --> 00:08:20,963
Mr. Jaypee and Miss Joan
are wearing blue...

89
00:08:20,963 --> 00:08:24,806
Oh, why does Miss Joyce
not have a partner?

90
00:08:25,973 --> 00:08:27,610
Don't worry. There's another one coming.

91
00:08:27,610 --> 00:08:29,211
Maybe we should just wait for him.

92
00:08:29,211 --> 00:08:31,280
- Maybe...
- Sir, sir.

93
00:08:31,280 --> 00:08:33,682
- I'm sorry, I'm late.
- You're right on time.

94
00:08:40,088 --> 00:08:42,624
Please wear this, Mr. Liam.

95
00:08:42,624 --> 00:08:46,327
So you will be Miss Joyce's buddy
for this tour.

96
00:08:48,229 --> 00:08:50,432
So you're part of this tour, too?

97
00:08:51,970 --> 00:08:53,975
Do you know each other?

98
00:08:55,723 --> 00:08:57,324
Very well.

99
00:08:58,640 --> 00:09:00,075
Okay, follow me.

100
00:09:00,075 --> 00:09:01,776
Let's start the tour.

101
00:09:01,776 --> 00:09:03,077
Come on.

102
00:09:04,979 --> 00:09:11,085
You can't escape me this time,
like what you did yesterday.

103
00:09:12,821 --> 00:09:15,657
I didn't escape from you.

104
00:09:15,657 --> 00:09:17,993
You were busy with your phone, remember?

105
00:09:18,922 --> 00:09:23,765
Yeah. I need to take care of
something at work back home.

106
00:09:23,765 --> 00:09:26,601
Work? But you call her love.

107
00:09:26,601 --> 00:09:28,670
What did you say, Joyce?

108
00:09:30,338 --> 00:09:31,639
Nothing.

109
00:09:32,607 --> 00:09:35,819
Mr. Liam, Miss Joyce, let's go.

110
00:09:35,819 --> 00:09:38,512
Oui. S'il vous plait.

111
00:09:51,758 --> 00:09:55,317
This is one of my personal favorites
here in Paris.

112
00:09:55,317 --> 00:09:59,647
The Pont Alexandre III,
or Alexander III Bridge.

113
00:09:59,647 --> 00:10:02,561
This was a gift from Russia to France

114
00:10:02,561 --> 00:10:06,541
as a symbol of their strong friendship
and alliance.

115
00:10:06,541 --> 00:10:11,041
It only proves that in love,
everything is possible.

116
00:10:11,869 --> 00:10:18,152
So no one should give up
when there are challenges.

117
00:10:18,152 --> 00:10:20,256
Well said, Miss Joyce.

118
00:10:20,256 --> 00:10:24,666
But you should know
when to give up a fight.

119
00:10:24,666 --> 00:10:27,230
I agree, especially if it's a losing game.

120
00:10:27,230 --> 00:10:29,655
You should concede.

121
00:10:32,402 --> 00:10:40,142
Sir Liam, what kind of fights
should we give up?

122
00:10:40,943 --> 00:10:44,213
The fight where you feel you're alone.

123
00:11:02,731 --> 00:11:05,700
Maybe we should take a lunch break.
I'll give you an hour.

124
00:11:05,700 --> 00:11:07,369
You're free to roam around.

125
00:11:07,369 --> 00:11:09,039
There are restaurants near here.

126
00:11:09,039 --> 00:11:11,640
And let's see each other in the van.

127
00:11:11,640 --> 00:11:13,309
But please, be on time.

128
00:11:13,309 --> 00:11:15,611
And you should stick together.

129
00:11:15,611 --> 00:11:17,459
Okay?

130
00:11:17,459 --> 00:11:19,081
Hey.

131
00:11:19,081 --> 00:11:21,124
We should stick together.

132
00:11:23,319 --> 00:11:26,422
Can we just meet by the van?

133
00:11:26,422 --> 00:11:29,256
I'll roam around alone.

134
00:11:30,217 --> 00:11:33,362
I also researched about Paris.

135
00:11:33,362 --> 00:11:35,461
Do you want me to give you a tour?

136
00:11:36,665 --> 00:11:39,502
It's my dream to be here, Liam.

137
00:11:39,502 --> 00:11:42,304
I know everything that you will say.

138
00:11:42,304 --> 00:11:44,373
Wow. Okay.

139
00:11:44,373 --> 00:11:45,883
We'll see.

140
00:11:46,842 --> 00:11:51,514
Did you know that there
are 32 candelabras here?

141
00:11:51,514 --> 00:11:55,785
So imagine how bright this place is
during night-time.

142
00:11:55,785 --> 00:12:03,775
And there are also sea creatures and cherubs.

143
00:12:03,775 --> 00:12:09,198
But if I were Engineers Résal and Alby,

144
00:12:09,198 --> 00:12:13,369
I would make a monument for
the most beautiful woman I've ever met.

145
00:12:15,805 --> 00:12:17,760
Are you trying to piss me off?

146
00:12:18,641 --> 00:12:21,549
You're so serious. I'm just happy.

147
00:12:22,678 --> 00:12:26,214
You deserve a monument

148
00:12:26,214 --> 00:12:29,213
for all the good things you've done
through your foundation.

149
00:12:30,276 --> 00:12:32,549
So you really are teasing me.

150
00:12:35,010 --> 00:12:39,695
Life's greatest happiness
is to be convinced we are loved.

151
00:12:39,695 --> 00:12:41,072
What?

152
00:12:42,252 --> 00:12:46,235
It's not good if you're just
convincing yourself, right?

153
00:12:46,235 --> 00:12:48,439
Especially if you're the only one fighting.

154
00:12:49,271 --> 00:12:50,971
Liam, wait.

155
00:12:51,874 --> 00:12:55,611
What is with the insinuations?

156
00:12:55,611 --> 00:12:57,780
Is that about our past?

157
00:12:57,780 --> 00:12:59,128
Wait.

158
00:12:59,128 --> 00:13:01,097
Why are you blaming me?

159
00:13:01,097 --> 00:13:06,134
It's one of the famous quotes of
the romantic writer, Victor Hugo.

160
00:13:07,549 --> 00:13:09,939
Is your name Victor?

161
00:13:11,527 --> 00:13:13,970
I'm just kidding.

162
00:13:14,897 --> 00:13:17,142
But you know what, Joyce?

163
00:13:19,802 --> 00:13:23,706
I want to tell you so many things
you don't know yet.

164
00:13:39,455 --> 00:13:40,978
Hello, love?

165
00:13:42,791 --> 00:13:44,392
Yes.

166
00:13:45,928 --> 00:13:48,416
- Yes...
- Love, my foot.

167
00:14:01,741 --> 00:14:03,142
<i>Yes, Joyce?</i>

168
00:14:03,142 --> 00:14:05,014
<i>What's the problem this time?</i>

169
00:14:05,014 --> 00:14:07,550
My gosh, Odet.
How can I have fun here?

170
00:14:07,550 --> 00:14:11,954
Of all people, it's Liam who I encountered
here in Paris.

171
00:14:11,954 --> 00:14:15,057
He did nothing but piss me off the whole day.

172
00:14:15,057 --> 00:14:17,393
<i>What did he do to you?</i>

173
00:14:17,393 --> 00:14:22,197
All he did was say things
about our failed marriage.

174
00:14:22,197 --> 00:14:27,235
I thought it was a mutual decision
when you separated?

175
00:14:28,170 --> 00:14:30,639
I'll back out from this tour
if I lose my patience.

176
00:14:30,639 --> 00:14:33,375
Can I just return to Manila?

177
00:14:33,375 --> 00:14:37,977
<i>Go alone if you're really pissed off.</i>

178
00:14:37,977 --> 00:14:41,569
<i>Admit it. You want to be with Liam, too!</i>

179
00:14:41,569 --> 00:14:47,514
You meet Liam out of all the million people
in Paris.

180
00:14:47,514 --> 00:14:50,526
Fate really has its own way!

181
00:14:50,526 --> 00:14:57,666
Please tell "fate" not to interfere
with my moving on!

182
00:14:57,666 --> 00:15:00,833
Joyce, may I remind you,

183
00:15:00,833 --> 00:15:04,738
I'm not your marriage and family therapist.

184
00:15:04,738 --> 00:15:09,042
I'm your foundation's secretary.

185
00:15:09,042 --> 00:15:10,577
Okay, Joyce?

186
00:15:10,577 --> 00:15:12,812
<i>Aside from putting on my makeup,</i>

187
00:15:12,812 --> 00:15:14,449
I have prepared everything for the mountains

188
00:15:14,449 --> 00:15:16,410
you will climb to give out school supplies.

189
00:15:19,520 --> 00:15:22,389
<i>What happened to you?</i>

190
00:15:22,389 --> 00:15:23,799
Odet, wait...

191
00:15:25,485 --> 00:15:27,386
Where am I?

192
00:15:28,595 --> 00:15:32,032
Odet, I'm lost! I don't know where I am.

193
00:15:32,032 --> 00:15:35,068
<i>What? My gosh, Joyce!</i>

194
00:15:37,037 --> 00:15:40,308
Wait, where's Miss Joyce?

195
00:15:40,308 --> 00:15:41,676
I also don't know.

196
00:15:41,676 --> 00:15:45,179
Every time I talk to someone on the phone,
she goes missing.

197
00:15:45,179 --> 00:15:48,816
I told you there's a buddy system.
You should stick with each other.

198
00:15:48,816 --> 00:15:49,917
What do we do now?

199
00:15:49,917 --> 00:15:53,080
I'm sorry, Sir. Don't worry...

200
00:15:53,080 --> 00:15:54,989
I'll look for her.

201
00:15:54,989 --> 00:15:57,091
I won't go with you
to your last destination.

202
00:15:57,091 --> 00:15:59,560
Okay, let us know
if you find Miss Joyce, okay?

203
00:15:59,560 --> 00:16:01,596
- Okay. Be safe.
- Be safe, too.

204
00:16:01,596 --> 00:16:03,530
Let's go.

205
00:16:06,033 --> 00:16:08,693
Where did you go, Joyce?

206
00:16:21,949 --> 00:16:23,591
Joyce!

207
00:16:26,287 --> 00:16:27,955
Joyce, come on!

208
00:16:27,955 --> 00:16:31,358
Where have you been?
We've been looking for you.

209
00:16:36,851 --> 00:16:38,800
I went to get some fresh air.

210
00:16:38,800 --> 00:16:40,968
Get some fresh air?

211
00:16:40,968 --> 00:16:42,904
We shouldn't leave each other, Joyce.

212
00:16:42,904 --> 00:16:46,140
Why do you keep leaving me alone?

213
00:16:46,140 --> 00:16:47,975
Let's go.

214
00:16:47,975 --> 00:16:49,910
You're funny.

215
00:16:50,945 --> 00:16:53,080
What's your problem?

216
00:16:54,882 --> 00:16:57,151
Is this what you want, Liam?

217
00:16:59,620 --> 00:17:05,426
Fine, let's speak in innuendos.

218
00:17:07,648 --> 00:17:09,642
Tell me.

219
00:17:11,165 --> 00:17:13,134
Was I really the one who left?

220
00:17:13,134 --> 00:17:14,735
Joyce...

221
00:17:14,735 --> 00:17:17,037
Why? That's the truth.

222
00:17:18,673 --> 00:17:21,943
Liam, who wanted to break us up?

223
00:17:21,943 --> 00:17:25,913
Joyce, my only point is,
you went missing while I was on the phone.

224
00:17:25,913 --> 00:17:27,415
That's all.

225
00:17:27,415 --> 00:17:30,117
Stop gaslighting me, Liam.

226
00:17:31,118 --> 00:17:33,454
Stop it. Tell me everything you want to say!

227
00:17:33,454 --> 00:17:35,647
Get straight to the point!

228
00:17:36,757 --> 00:17:39,493
This confrontation is already
three years overdue, anyway.

229
00:17:39,493 --> 00:17:44,565
To be fair,
you even chose such a beautiful location!

230
00:17:49,470 --> 00:17:51,439
Okay, Joyce.

231
00:17:51,439 --> 00:17:53,507
What do you want to talk about?

232
00:17:53,507 --> 00:17:54,803
Tell me.

233
00:17:55,443 --> 00:17:59,817
I want to talk about us, Liam.

234
00:18:03,551 --> 00:18:06,753
I want to understand why you're mad at me.

235
00:18:10,157 --> 00:18:12,356
Tell me everything.

236
00:18:15,066 --> 00:18:16,961
Okay, Joyce.

237
00:18:18,065 --> 00:18:21,211
I'll admit that when I saw you here...

238
00:18:22,470 --> 00:18:25,133
I felt embarrassed.

239
00:18:26,374 --> 00:18:30,211
Seeing you reminded me of all my mistakes!

240
00:18:30,211 --> 00:18:34,469
All my shortcomings!
That it was my fault that our son died!

241
00:18:35,383 --> 00:18:39,961
Liam, you're not the only one
who suffered when Dex died.

242
00:18:41,222 --> 00:18:44,525
I thought we would grieve together.

243
00:18:46,172 --> 00:18:50,438
I thought we would go through it together.
But what did you do?

244
00:18:51,884 --> 00:18:54,953
What did you do? You left me!

245
00:18:58,039 --> 00:19:03,310
Liam, I knew that I shouldn't give up on you.

246
00:19:05,513 --> 00:19:07,790
It was hard, Liam.

247
00:19:11,806 --> 00:19:15,089
You don't know how hard it was, Liam.

248
00:19:17,024 --> 00:19:20,661
Liam, it was so painful when I lost my child.

249
00:19:22,730 --> 00:19:26,467
It's also painful that I lost a husband.

250
00:19:28,424 --> 00:19:33,354
For the last time, before we separate...

251
00:19:35,576 --> 00:19:38,705
let's try not to fight.

252
00:20:17,987 --> 00:20:19,495
Here.

253
00:20:23,691 --> 00:20:25,480
Thank you.

254
00:20:26,927 --> 00:20:29,766
Can we start the tour again?

255
00:20:31,799 --> 00:20:33,444
You're right.

256
00:20:35,770 --> 00:20:40,007
If this is where we end things...

257
00:20:40,007 --> 00:20:42,626
we should at least end it happily.

258
00:20:53,187 --> 00:20:57,626
Your ice cream might turn salty
because of your tears.

259
00:21:04,031 --> 00:21:06,067
Try it.

260
00:21:06,067 --> 00:21:07,368
Yes, it's salty.

261
00:21:07,368 --> 00:21:08,927
Salty?

262
00:21:08,927 --> 00:21:10,638
I told you.

263
00:21:10,638 --> 00:21:12,636
Your tears.

264
00:21:13,433 --> 00:21:15,909
You should have this.

265
00:21:16,573 --> 00:21:18,042
Why?

266
00:21:20,981 --> 00:21:23,492
So you can taste my sadness.

267
00:21:25,920 --> 00:21:29,323
Joyce, we don't have to be sad.

268
00:21:29,323 --> 00:21:32,526
Honestly, I'm happy.

269
00:21:32,526 --> 00:21:35,830
Because, finally, after three years,

270
00:21:35,830 --> 00:21:42,236
we let out our resentments
towards each other.

271
00:21:42,236 --> 00:21:45,450
So, are we okay now?

272
00:21:51,545 --> 00:21:53,581
How can we be okay?

273
00:21:53,581 --> 00:21:57,028
We're no longer part of the tour.
Where do we go now?

274
00:21:58,419 --> 00:22:01,088
We can make our own itinerary.

275
00:22:01,088 --> 00:22:02,528
Come on.

276
00:22:03,710 --> 00:22:06,112
Where are we going?

277
00:22:13,367 --> 00:22:15,636
Joyce, hurry up.

278
00:22:15,636 --> 00:22:18,606
Liam, wait. We've been walking forever.

279
00:22:18,606 --> 00:22:19,874
Where are we going?

280
00:22:19,874 --> 00:22:21,475
You will like this.

281
00:22:21,475 --> 00:22:23,444
Wait.

282
00:22:23,444 --> 00:22:26,614
Excuse me. I'm wearing heels.

283
00:22:26,614 --> 00:22:27,915
My feet hurt already.

284
00:22:27,915 --> 00:22:29,650
Come on. Hurry up!

285
00:22:29,650 --> 00:22:31,385
Let's go!

286
00:22:31,385 --> 00:22:32,553
You can do it.

287
00:22:32,553 --> 00:22:34,288
Liam.

288
00:22:34,288 --> 00:22:36,390
Why did you wear heels?

289
00:22:36,390 --> 00:22:38,532
Because this is Paris!

290
00:22:39,226 --> 00:22:40,665
Come on!

291
00:22:43,230 --> 00:22:45,266
Let's go. Hurry!

292
00:22:46,433 --> 00:22:49,069
You will be surprised
with what I will show you.

293
00:22:49,069 --> 00:22:50,938
What is it?

294
00:22:50,938 --> 00:22:52,446
Just wait.

295
00:22:55,609 --> 00:22:57,202
Here.

296
00:23:10,925 --> 00:23:14,795
Welcome to the bridge of romance.

297
00:23:21,602 --> 00:23:23,604
It's so beautiful.

298
00:23:25,439 --> 00:23:29,309
Eiffel Tower isn't the only beautiful thing
here in Paris.

299
00:23:32,179 --> 00:23:33,981
Joyce...

300
00:23:35,282 --> 00:23:41,372
I realized that a story isn't whole
if it's only one-sided.

301
00:23:44,892 --> 00:23:48,187
There are many reasons why
I should ask your forgiveness.

302
00:23:51,332 --> 00:23:58,238
I also realized that I was
so focused on my own suffering.

303
00:24:01,008 --> 00:24:04,003
Maybe that's why I gave up on us.

304
00:24:07,982 --> 00:24:14,654
I forgot about our happy memories together.

305
00:24:16,390 --> 00:24:25,728
I forgot how happy I was
when I was with you.

306
00:24:27,434 --> 00:24:30,277
I forgot to look at the bigger picture.

307
00:24:31,705 --> 00:24:34,908
<i>I shouldn't have let anger
get the better of me.</i>

308
00:24:34,908 --> 00:24:37,244
<i>I wish I didn't leave you.</i>

309
00:24:37,244 --> 00:24:41,147
<i>I wish we faced together Dex's passing.</i>

310
00:24:42,850 --> 00:24:45,886
Liam, there's something I want to tell you.

311
00:24:49,757 --> 00:24:51,859
Joyce...

312
00:24:51,859 --> 00:24:55,929
If it will only make me sad...

313
00:24:55,929 --> 00:24:58,300
can you not say it anymore?

314
00:25:01,035 --> 00:25:05,152
Can you let me be happy this time?

315
00:25:06,774 --> 00:25:10,944
So I'll have happy memories before I...

316
00:25:12,279 --> 00:25:13,827
before I set you free.

317
00:25:18,252 --> 00:25:21,892
<i>If only I could stop the hands of time.</i>

318
00:25:25,926 --> 00:25:27,713
Hurry up!

319
00:25:37,438 --> 00:25:40,240
<i>If only I could, Liam.</i>

320
00:25:40,240 --> 00:25:42,115
<i>I would do it.</i>

321
00:26:07,267 --> 00:26:09,370
Liam, can I ask you a question?

322
00:26:09,370 --> 00:26:10,740
What is it?

323
00:26:13,974 --> 00:26:17,678
No, never mind.

324
00:26:17,678 --> 00:26:18,779
What is it?

325
00:26:18,779 --> 00:26:20,447
Come on, Joyce...

326
00:26:20,447 --> 00:26:21,815
Tell me, what is it?

327
00:26:21,815 --> 00:26:23,617
Never mind.

328
00:26:23,617 --> 00:26:26,319
What is it? Tell me.

329
00:26:28,555 --> 00:26:31,007
The one you call "love".

330
00:26:32,860 --> 00:26:34,514
Love...

331
00:26:36,397 --> 00:26:41,576
Well, wait. Where do I start?

332
00:26:46,640 --> 00:26:47,975
- Liam.
- Yes?

333
00:26:47,975 --> 00:26:51,044
Champ de Mars is so big.

334
00:26:51,044 --> 00:26:54,982
You can start from the beginning.

335
00:26:54,982 --> 00:26:56,791
Okay, fine.

336
00:26:56,791 --> 00:27:00,475
Love is a good person.

337
00:27:00,475 --> 00:27:02,310
She's always happy.

338
00:27:04,987 --> 00:27:06,598
Is she pretty?

339
00:27:08,739 --> 00:27:10,664
Yes, she is.

340
00:27:10,664 --> 00:27:12,166
Hardworking.

341
00:27:12,166 --> 00:27:14,001
Diligent.

342
00:27:14,001 --> 00:27:18,138
Most of all, you can always ask her a favor.

343
00:27:20,874 --> 00:27:22,434
What?

344
00:27:24,450 --> 00:27:33,053
Love is my co-teacher
at the university where I teach.

345
00:27:33,053 --> 00:27:38,459
She's Professor Lovely de Leon,
also known as Love.

346
00:27:38,459 --> 00:27:45,319
She's taking all my teaching loads
while I'm on leave.

347
00:27:46,633 --> 00:27:49,903
Love is your co-worker?

348
00:27:49,903 --> 00:27:51,428
Yes.

349
00:27:55,709 --> 00:27:57,277
But are you together?

350
00:27:57,277 --> 00:27:59,379
What do you mean?

351
00:27:59,379 --> 00:28:02,616
Come on. Love is already married.

352
00:28:02,616 --> 00:28:04,318
Wait...

353
00:28:04,318 --> 00:28:07,929
Was that why you walked out on me?

354
00:28:07,929 --> 00:28:11,391
Oh, Joyce!

355
00:28:11,391 --> 00:28:12,926
Are you jealous?

356
00:28:12,926 --> 00:28:14,228
Excuse me?

357
00:28:14,228 --> 00:28:15,295
Wow!

358
00:28:15,295 --> 00:28:17,331
I'm not...

359
00:28:17,331 --> 00:28:19,383
I'm not jealous.

360
00:28:20,219 --> 00:28:23,303
I no longer have the right to get jealous.

361
00:28:23,303 --> 00:28:25,074
Do you want me to give it to you?

362
00:28:25,906 --> 00:28:27,241
Give me what?

363
00:28:27,241 --> 00:28:29,331
The right to get jealous.

364
00:28:34,014 --> 00:28:35,749
I couldn't ask for more, Liam.

365
00:28:35,749 --> 00:28:38,167
So don't make my hopes up.

366
00:28:39,620 --> 00:28:44,258
What matters is we were given
a chance to start over again.

367
00:28:44,258 --> 00:28:46,126
Start over again?

368
00:28:46,126 --> 00:28:47,585
Yes.

369
00:28:52,266 --> 00:28:54,007
Think about it.

370
00:28:54,935 --> 00:29:00,440
This is where I found the old Liam...

371
00:29:00,440 --> 00:29:02,843
in Paris, France.

372
00:29:04,311 --> 00:29:07,681
The Liam...

373
00:29:07,681 --> 00:29:09,782
I admired.

374
00:29:10,864 --> 00:29:14,108
The Liam who has confidence in himself.

375
00:29:15,322 --> 00:29:18,885
The Liam I entrusted my life with.

376
00:29:19,793 --> 00:29:21,979
Don't you have any regrets?

377
00:29:23,061 --> 00:29:25,783
After all that we've been through?

378
00:29:27,234 --> 00:29:28,822
Nothing.

379
00:29:31,004 --> 00:29:36,853
Dex wouldn't want us to live
a life full of regrets and anger.

380
00:29:40,714 --> 00:29:42,482
I'm sorry.

381
00:29:42,482 --> 00:29:45,485
Sorry, we should be happy.

382
00:29:45,485 --> 00:29:48,688
Come on. You don't have to apologize.

383
00:29:50,490 --> 00:29:52,549
Honestly, I'm happy.

384
00:29:53,560 --> 00:29:57,051
I'm happy to hear everything you said.

385
00:29:58,065 --> 00:30:03,536
Maybe that's what
I've been wanting to hear...

386
00:30:04,780 --> 00:30:07,962
That I can live without regrets.

387
00:30:09,276 --> 00:30:12,569
Liam, it's hard to live...

388
00:30:13,714 --> 00:30:20,653
with a desire to change something
in your past.

389
00:30:23,256 --> 00:30:26,651
We only have the future.

390
00:30:31,031 --> 00:30:33,132
Joyce, sorry.

391
00:30:34,534 --> 00:30:36,536
What for?

392
00:30:38,305 --> 00:30:40,288
Sorry that I left you.

393
00:30:43,543 --> 00:30:46,178
Sorry, too, because...

394
00:30:48,660 --> 00:30:50,380
Because?

395
00:30:51,629 --> 00:30:54,136
I can't help it.

396
00:30:56,770 --> 00:30:59,605
You can't help what?

397
00:31:11,905 --> 00:31:13,808
I still love you.

398
00:31:16,071 --> 00:31:18,222
Until now...

399
00:31:20,080 --> 00:31:21,957
you're still the one.

400
00:32:48,268 --> 00:32:50,837
<i>If only I could rewrite my story...</i>

401
00:32:50,837 --> 00:32:53,373
<i>I wish I was a star.</i>

402
00:32:53,373 --> 00:32:57,580
<i>So I could have spent
millions of years with them.</i>

403
00:33:01,748 --> 00:33:05,423
Liam, are you okay?
What's going on with you?

404
00:33:07,736 --> 00:33:10,357
- Joyce...
- Liam?

405
00:33:10,357 --> 00:33:12,192
Joyce.

406
00:33:12,192 --> 00:33:15,650
Joyce, I dreamed of everything.

407
00:33:17,998 --> 00:33:22,035
The typewriter changed our life, Joyce.
I saw everything.

408
00:33:22,035 --> 00:33:24,971
I remembered everything.

409
00:33:24,971 --> 00:33:26,973
Joyce, I need to find the typewriter.

410
00:33:26,973 --> 00:33:28,909
I need to bring Dex back to life!

411
00:33:28,909 --> 00:33:31,378
- I need to bring Dex back to life, Joyce!
- I threw the typewriter away.

412
00:33:31,378 --> 00:33:34,881
- It's gone.
- Joyce, why did you throw it away?

413
00:33:34,881 --> 00:33:37,818
I need to bring Dex back to life!

414
00:33:37,818 --> 00:33:39,052
Liam.

415
00:33:39,052 --> 00:33:40,787
That is not the solution, Liam.

416
00:33:40,787 --> 00:33:44,324
Joyce... Joyce, why...
Why did you bring us back here?

417
00:33:44,324 --> 00:33:48,395
Why did you bring us back to the point
where I'm writing?

418
00:33:48,395 --> 00:33:51,331
Why didn't you...
Why didn't you bring Dex back to life?

419
00:33:51,331 --> 00:33:54,901
You know there is a price to pay!

420
00:33:54,901 --> 00:33:58,438
We don't need the typewriter, Liam.

421
00:33:58,438 --> 00:34:00,273
The solution lies in how we will stay strong

422
00:34:00,273 --> 00:34:04,778
despite all the tragedies in our life!

423
00:34:04,778 --> 00:34:08,114
The two of us, not the typewriter!

424
00:34:15,422 --> 00:34:17,701
I'm sorry, Joyce.

425
00:34:20,594 --> 00:34:22,503
I understand.

426
00:34:24,464 --> 00:34:27,149
I understand everything you said.

427
00:34:28,201 --> 00:34:30,704
Now...

428
00:34:30,704 --> 00:34:36,514
all we can do is be strong for Dex.

429
00:34:40,981 --> 00:34:44,451
Let's make our son's life meaningful.

430
00:34:45,719 --> 00:34:47,456
Joyce...

431
00:34:51,853 --> 00:34:54,253
I love you so much.

432
00:34:56,321 --> 00:34:57,573
So much.

433
00:34:59,699 --> 00:35:01,292
So much.

434
00:35:07,240 --> 00:35:10,433
I love you so much, too, Liam.

435
00:35:14,981 --> 00:35:18,272
I love you in whatever world we are in.

436
00:35:34,501 --> 00:35:36,336
I love you so much.

437
00:36:02,529 --> 00:36:05,086
I miss our kid.

438
00:36:12,205 --> 00:36:15,224
I'm sure he's happy now.

439
00:37:10,334 --> 00:37:12,359
[Via dela Peña rocking at the Fashion Week
in the city of love!]

440
00:37:13,800 --> 00:37:15,950
Via's here?

441
00:37:32,619 --> 00:37:35,189
Liam, do you want to go?

442
00:37:42,896 --> 00:37:45,936
I promise, I won't let go of your hand.

443
00:38:13,742 --> 00:38:18,703
Luckily, Mrs. Malvarosa knows
the organizer of this event.

444
00:38:20,162 --> 00:38:22,964
She got us on the guest list.

445
00:38:24,190 --> 00:38:25,936
Let's go?

446
00:38:25,936 --> 00:38:27,770
Yes.

447
00:38:28,775 --> 00:38:30,944
- You enjoyed it?
- Yes, we did.

448
00:38:30,944 --> 00:38:34,680
Thank you so much for coming.
I appreciate you, guys.

449
00:38:37,297 --> 00:38:39,387
Sorry, bro.

450
00:38:42,754 --> 00:38:44,194
Wait.

451
00:38:48,191 --> 00:38:51,963
I'm Attorney Hans Arevalo.

452
00:38:51,963 --> 00:38:55,468
I'm from Taguig. Here's my card.

453
00:38:55,468 --> 00:38:57,303
Liam Herrera.

454
00:38:57,303 --> 00:38:58,371
Liam, nice to meet you.

455
00:38:58,371 --> 00:39:00,239
Nice to meet you, too.

456
00:39:01,141 --> 00:39:02,838
I'm Joyce.

457
00:39:03,723 --> 00:39:06,033
Joycelyn Trinidad.

458
00:39:07,127 --> 00:39:10,583
Do you know my girlfriend?

459
00:39:10,583 --> 00:39:12,275
Girlfriend?

460
00:39:12,986 --> 00:39:14,921
- There she is.
- Hi, love!

461
00:39:14,921 --> 00:39:16,439
Hello, love.

462
00:39:21,217 --> 00:39:23,219
Wait, who are they?

463
00:39:24,230 --> 00:39:26,230
Sorry, I thought you knew each other.

464
00:39:26,230 --> 00:39:29,733
But they're also Filipinos.

465
00:39:33,573 --> 00:39:35,511
Sorry, have we met?

466
00:39:38,081 --> 00:39:42,182
No, actually,
we're just here to watch the fashion show.

467
00:39:42,182 --> 00:39:46,352
We're proud to see a fellow Filipino
in the Paris Fashion Week.

468
00:39:46,352 --> 00:39:47,716
Thank you.

469
00:39:47,716 --> 00:39:49,097
Via.

470
00:39:50,524 --> 00:39:52,105
Joyce.

471
00:39:53,193 --> 00:39:54,494
Liam.

472
00:39:54,494 --> 00:39:58,425
It's nice to meet you both, Joyce and Liam.

473
00:39:59,222 --> 00:40:04,436
I hope we can go out together
when we return to the Philippines.

474
00:40:05,138 --> 00:40:06,706
That's so nice of you.

475
00:40:06,706 --> 00:40:08,141
Yes, sure.

476
00:40:08,141 --> 00:40:09,842
We should take a photo.

477
00:40:09,842 --> 00:40:11,995
Yes? Shall we?

478
00:40:13,111 --> 00:40:14,878
Okay.

479
00:40:25,625 --> 00:40:27,060
Thank you.

480
00:40:27,060 --> 00:40:29,355
- Thank you.
- Merci.

481
00:40:32,732 --> 00:40:35,739
So, let's see each other in Manila?

482
00:40:35,739 --> 00:40:37,339
Of course.

483
00:40:38,738 --> 00:40:40,173
Nice to meet you, guys.

484
00:40:40,173 --> 00:40:41,714
Nice to meet you.

485
00:40:42,675 --> 00:40:46,294
Congratulations again, Miss Via.

486
00:40:46,294 --> 00:40:48,314
Merci beaucoup.

487
00:40:48,314 --> 00:40:51,184
I really appreciate you guys coming here.

488
00:40:51,184 --> 00:40:53,086
So, we'll just go around.

489
00:40:53,086 --> 00:40:54,892
Au revoir.

490
00:40:54,892 --> 00:40:56,281
Be safe.

491
00:41:02,095 --> 00:41:05,582
What just happened here?

492
00:41:07,433 --> 00:41:09,269
I don't know, either.

493
00:41:10,103 --> 00:41:11,371
So?

494
00:41:11,371 --> 00:41:12,910
- Let's go?
- Let's go?

495
00:41:23,648 --> 00:41:25,183
[Fashion Week plus running around with Hans:
The Paris Adventure!]

496
00:41:26,552 --> 00:41:30,276
I didn't look for them in this life.

497
00:41:32,292 --> 00:41:35,016
I thought...

498
00:41:35,016 --> 00:41:40,033
it would be unfair to you
if I focused on them.

499
00:41:40,033 --> 00:41:43,289
You didn't even meet them.

500
00:41:46,306 --> 00:41:48,107
You know what?

501
00:41:48,107 --> 00:41:50,276
I'm happy.

502
00:41:50,276 --> 00:41:53,046
I'm glad everything went well

503
00:41:53,046 --> 00:41:55,869
because I didn't use the typewriter.

504
00:41:56,689 --> 00:42:00,064
It's time for us to be happy.

505
00:42:02,221 --> 00:42:04,744
I told you.

506
00:42:06,626 --> 00:42:09,415
Our time will come.

507
00:42:11,998 --> 00:42:15,515
I'm happy that
after everything that happened,

508
00:42:17,344 --> 00:42:20,422
you're still the right one for me.

509
00:42:43,630 --> 00:42:45,088
Let's go?

510
00:42:54,636 --> 00:42:58,713
<i>What's the meaning of "the right one"?</i>

511
00:42:59,946 --> 00:43:02,431
I love you so much, Tess.
[Teresita N. Buenaventura]

512
00:43:03,716 --> 00:43:06,291
I hope you can forgive me...

513
00:43:08,388 --> 00:43:11,916
for not being brave.

514
00:43:15,832 --> 00:43:19,300
I hope my love for you can reach the heavens.

515
00:43:25,872 --> 00:43:32,022
<i>Is the right one the person who owns up
to his mistake and shortcomings?</i>

516
00:43:34,046 --> 00:43:37,884
Love, do I now look pretty on camera?

517
00:43:37,884 --> 00:43:39,436
Wait.

518
00:43:41,587 --> 00:43:42,922
It should be like that.

519
00:43:42,922 --> 00:43:44,056
Come on, love!

520
00:43:44,056 --> 00:43:45,240
You're perfect.

521
00:43:45,925 --> 00:43:49,061
You're always perfect, especially for me.

522
00:43:49,061 --> 00:43:51,931
- You're flattering me.
- <i>Is it the person who's willing to forgive?</i>

523
00:43:51,931 --> 00:43:54,600
It makes me giddy. It's effective!

524
00:43:54,600 --> 00:43:56,736
Okay. Let's start.

525
00:43:56,736 --> 00:43:58,704
Hello, mommies!

526
00:43:58,704 --> 00:44:03,609
Happy mommies and happy wives like me!

527
00:44:03,609 --> 00:44:05,845
How are you guys?

528
00:44:05,845 --> 00:44:07,747
<i>Is it the one who makes amends</i>
[Santo Cristo Park project is a gift]

529
00:44:07,747 --> 00:44:11,350
<i>when given a second chance?</i>
[from our beloved mayor, Ramon dela Peña]

530
00:44:11,350 --> 00:44:14,353
Don't put my face and name on it.

531
00:44:14,353 --> 00:44:16,152
Sorry, Mayor. Don't worry.

532
00:44:16,152 --> 00:44:22,228
We will strictly implement your instructions
on your next projects, sir.

533
00:44:22,228 --> 00:44:23,928
I will have it removed.

534
00:44:23,928 --> 00:44:25,479
That's enough.

535
00:44:26,265 --> 00:44:27,467
<i>Hello, Borj.</i>
[My Hoodlum Lover]

536
00:44:27,467 --> 00:44:30,436
<i>Why did you use that font for the poster?</i>

537
00:44:30,436 --> 00:44:33,306
Isn't that what we agreed on?

538
00:44:33,306 --> 00:44:34,907
- You said...
- <i>Okay, okay.</i>

539
00:44:34,907 --> 00:44:36,876
<i>I will look at it again when I get there.</i>

540
00:44:36,876 --> 00:44:38,478
- Okay. Make it faster.
- <i>I'm on my way there.</i>

541
00:44:38,478 --> 00:44:39,479
See you.

542
00:44:39,479 --> 00:44:40,713
<i>Okay, bye.</i>

543
00:44:40,713 --> 00:44:43,049
Come on. Stop arguing.

544
00:44:43,049 --> 00:44:45,818
We can talk about it and revise it.

545
00:44:45,818 --> 00:44:49,455
That's right. Chill.

546
00:44:49,455 --> 00:44:50,932
Okay.

547
00:44:53,626 --> 00:44:55,294
- Hey!
- Guys.

548
00:44:55,294 --> 00:44:56,896
I brought palabok.

549
00:44:56,896 --> 00:44:58,472
Wow!

550
00:44:58,472 --> 00:45:03,569
But is it really for us, boss dude, or...

551
00:45:03,569 --> 00:45:05,269
for Miss Megan?

552
00:45:05,269 --> 00:45:07,173
- Actually...
- You're really hot!

553
00:45:07,173 --> 00:45:08,508
This is what I brought for Megan.

554
00:45:08,508 --> 00:45:09,909
- That's big.
- Oh, only for her.

555
00:45:09,909 --> 00:45:11,844
You can bring it home to your kid.

556
00:45:11,844 --> 00:45:15,822
Special palabok for the...

557
00:45:15,822 --> 00:45:16,849
Special someone!

558
00:45:16,849 --> 00:45:18,284
You got it right, Deedee!

559
00:45:18,284 --> 00:45:19,685
The two of you are really something else!

560
00:45:19,685 --> 00:45:21,654
Stop it. Come on.

561
00:45:21,654 --> 00:45:24,790
But thank you, Vergil,

562
00:45:24,790 --> 00:45:31,195
for approving my suggestion
to make the movie's lead star a female.

563
00:45:31,195 --> 00:45:35,140
<i>Is it the person who knows
to listen and understand?</i>

564
00:45:37,503 --> 00:45:40,540
Perfect! Super lovely!

565
00:45:40,540 --> 00:45:43,109
Thank you, my Cupcake Loves.

566
00:45:43,109 --> 00:45:45,758
Thank you for
the overflowing love and support.

567
00:45:45,758 --> 00:45:50,062
<i>Is it the person who will
accept you wholeheartedly?</i>

568
00:46:05,064 --> 00:46:08,467
<i>Whether you believe in fate or not...</i>

569
00:46:08,467 --> 00:46:12,071
<i>in whatever mystery or magic...</i>

570
00:46:12,071 --> 00:46:18,344
<i>the right one is the person you always choose
to be the right one for you.</i>

571
00:46:18,344 --> 00:46:22,081
<i>The one you choose to be with you forever...</i>

572
00:46:22,081 --> 00:46:26,418
<i>and in whatever version of your life.</i>

573
00:46:36,429 --> 00:46:39,699
<i>Mine and your mom's love story
still went through a lot.</i>

574
00:46:39,699 --> 00:46:44,270
<i>It is as unique as the love story
written by Ricky Lee.</i>

575
00:46:44,270 --> 00:46:48,541
<i>It wouldn't be complete
if we didn't meet you, Dex.</i>

576
00:46:48,541 --> 00:46:51,944
<i>Though you're not with us now...</i>

577
00:46:52,945 --> 00:46:55,314
<i>I hope you're proud of us.</i>

578
00:46:57,450 --> 00:47:04,356
<i>In the end, we stand by the person
who's the right one for us.</i>

579
00:47:05,625 --> 00:47:09,428
<i>I know you're one of the stars that guide us.</i>

580
00:47:09,428 --> 00:47:12,489
<i>We love you so much.</i>

581
00:48:16,312 --> 00:48:18,913
[The Write One: A Novel,
by William "Liam" Herrera]

582
00:48:23,602 --> 00:48:25,705
Junk!

583
00:48:25,705 --> 00:48:29,110
I buy and sell old stuff!
